@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] data-no-user-credentials
The phone talks to one server, the one set in Settings. The only credentials it holds are
the optional Cloudflare Access client ID and secret and the account's session, which are
sent only to that server, stored only on the phone, and never logged or shown back in
full. The account's password is sent once, to sign in, and never stored (Tavi, 16 Oct
12:47). The session MUST go only to the server address it signed in on, and the password
and session MUST NOT go over plain HTTP except to this phone or the emulator's host
(Devin Review on PR 58).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] data-settings-sync
While signed in, the phone's choices of look, language, layout, fonts, code size, sounds,
vibration, AI effort and Analyze, and which repositories the Inbox hides, are kept on the
account, each with when it changed, and the newer change of each wins; a change made while
a sync is out is never undone by it, and choices made before the first sync count as the
oldest, so they reach an account without them but never override another phone's. The server and its
Access secrets, the session, Update notifications and Usage stats stay on the phone
("start saving settings, both on the mobile app and also sync it": Tavi, 16 Oct 12:47).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] data-server-is-the-source
The phone reads pull requests, diffs, tours and AI work from its server's API, the same
actions the web app runs; it never calls GitHub or a model provider itself.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] data-lite-diffs
A large pull request opens from a `lite` diff: files past the patch budget arrive with no
hunks and `patchOmitted`, show skeletons where their code goes, and get their hunks from
`diff-patches` (rules 51 and 52; architecture, The phone reads the server's store).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] data-tours-are-kept
Tours the person has opened are stored on the phone, so they open at once the next time
(CHANGELOG 0.28.0).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] data-jev-polls-briefly
While Inbox rows lack Jev's read and the Inbox needs it, the phone reads `my-pulls-cached`
with `revalidate: false` and `classify: true` every three seconds for two minutes at most,
and never shows a loading screen for it (architecture, Jev; rule 51).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] data-file-marks-follow-the-head
The phone drops a diff's file marks when the pull request's head moves, and shows Jev's
read only for the current head and title (architecture, Jev).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] data-analytics-queue-on-disk
Every usage event the phone tracks MUST be written to `filesDir/analytics/queue.ndjson`
as well as kept in memory, so no network and a killed app lose nothing: a crash's own
event is written to that file on the crashing thread, and what is left goes up on the
next start or with a WorkManager job that waits for a network. The queue keeps at most
5,000 events, dropping the oldest, and sends them to `POST /api/events` on the server set
in Settings, with the same Access headers as `/api/rpc`, at most 200 a call. It MUST NOT
use any analytics, crash or telemetry package (message 15 Oct 20:58, "We will track them
directly on our server. No need for fancy packages", and 21:12, "doit"; plan "Pulls
analytics on our own server").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] data-analytics-counts-not-content
An event's props MUST carry only counts, timings, fixed choices, on or off values and a
pull request's repository and number. The phone MUST NOT send a file's name or path (a
file is its extension only), search or Ask text, a diff, code, a comment, an AI answer, a
title, a server address or any credential, and it drops every prop key the server would
drop (`AnalyticsRules.cleanProps`) before the event is queued. A screen is one of a fixed
set of lowercase words and a server call is its RPC name only, never its arguments. A
crash or a failed load carries only the error's class, its own message cut short, the top
frames of its stack and the screen (plan "Pulls analytics on our own server",
Guardrails; message 15 Oct 20:58).
